  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2019-p6.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "We can rewrite the left side as \\[(n+1)n!+(n+2)(n+1)n!\\]\\[=((n+2)^2-1)n!,\\] so \\[((n+2)^2-1) n! = 440 n!\\] Therefore, \\[(n+2)^2=441,\\] so \\(n=19.\\) The sum of its digits is \\(10.\\)\n\nThus, the answer is C .",
      "hints": [
        "Factor \\((n+1)!\\) and \\((n+2)!\\) in terms of \\(n!\\)",
        "Divide by \\(n!\\) and solve the resulting square equation"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
